WEBVTT

00:10:59.987 --> 00:11:01.600
and the energy crisis that caused

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:04.070
with stagnation and inflation
at the same time.

00:11:04.070 --> 00:11:05.533
Gerald Ford was president.

00:11:05.533 --> 00:11:09.117
And he realized that if we could double
the fuel efficiency of new vehicles,

00:11:09.117 --> 00:11:11.420
we could cut in half their energy use.

00:11:11.733 --> 00:11:14.363
So he signed a law
to double the fuel efficiency

00:11:14.363 --> 00:11:15.933
of new vehicles sold in America,

00:11:15.933 --> 00:11:18.550
from 13 miles per gallon,
absolutely pathetic,

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:19.700
to 26 miles per gallon.

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:20.967
JD: That's big.

00:11:20.967 --> 00:11:24.450
HH: It’s pathetic by today’s standards,
but it was a big deal then, right?

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:25.470
It was doubling.

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:30.597
But by setting a number as the goal,
we created a 25-year plateau.